<html class="js" lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}"{% if request.cookies['app_color_scheme'] == 'dark' %} data-theme="dark"{% endif %}>
  <head>
    {%- comment -%}
      AstroAura dark mode no-flash gate. MUST be the first thing in <head>,
      before any stylesheet/font, so it runs before first paint. It is
      authoritative over the SSR data-theme attr above (Shopify full-page-cache
      can serve a stale attr): it ADDS dark when the app cookie or the manual
      web choice says dark, and REMOVES a wrongly-cached dark attr otherwise.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script>
    (function(){try{
      // Dark mode ONLY via the Aura AI app cookie (app_color_scheme=dark). No
      // manual/web toggle anywhere else. Authoritative over the SSR attr.
      var dark = document.cookie.split('; ').indexOf('app_color_scheme=dark') > -1;
      var el = document.documentElement;
      if (dark) el.setAttribute('data-theme','dark'); else el.removeAttribute('data-theme');
    }catch(e){}})();
    </script>

    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover, interactive-widget=resizes-content">
    {%- comment -%} Turbo: render link-click navigations ONCE from the fresh
        response. The default cached-preview pass painted the destination at
        its old scroll position then re-rendered ("loads twice" + lands
        mid-page + jump to top). Back/forward restore still uses the cache. {%- endcomment -%}
    <meta name="turbo-cache-control" content="no-preview">
    {%- comment -%} AstroAura: the cart is the slide-up drawer only — kill the standalone /cart page {%- endcomment -%}
    <script>if(location.pathname.replace(/\/+$/,'')==='/cart'){location.replace('/?cart=open');}</script>
